  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that the RNA encoder choice is the dominant design variable: switching from PCA_n2000 to scvi_n200 (config_024→config_049) yielded a large ~8-point accuracy gain with all other settings held constant. The current best configuration (config_017: scvi_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted → 0.725 acc) has been reached, but scgpt has not been tested in any experiment. config_012 (scgpt, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) is a clean, single-variable swap against config_017, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder while keeping the image encoder, aggregation, and fusion at their best-performing values. This is the highest-information experiment available: if scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it falls short, it confirms scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder and redirects budget toward refining aggregation/fusion or image-encoder choices. No other untested configuration addresses this critical, unexplored variable as directly."
}

